Q: what is difference between {{}} and {% %} in django templates A: <p><code>{% %}</code> for <strong><code>IF ELSE CONDITIONS</code></strong> and FOR LOOP etc</p>
<p><code>{{ }}</code> for veriables that rendered from view function also used in FOR LOOP veriables like</p>
<pre><code>{% for obj in qs%}  
    {{ obj.veriable_name }}
{% endfor %}
</code></pre>

Q: How to mock a void method with PowerMockito? A: <p>The problem was my understanding :) </p>

<p>I changed signature of the method under test with following and could test it. So in this case I am passing instance of <code>ChatMsgDbAsyncHelper</code> to the method rather than create it within method.</p>

<pre><code>@VisibleForTesting
    void addNextScreenBasedOnBookingStatus(final Booking booking, final ChatMsgDbAsyncHelper chatMsgHelper) {
...
}
</code></pre>

<p>and test works fine now:</p>

<pre><code>@Test
public void addNextScreenBasedOnBookingStatus_whenBookingIsNull() throws Exception {
    ChatMsgDbAsyncHelper mChatMsgHelper = PowerMockito.spy(new ChatMsgDbAsyncHelper());
    doNothing().when(mChatMsgHelper).cleanAllMessages(any(Context.class));

    mNavBuilder.addNextScreenBasedOnBookingStatus(null, mChatMsgHelper);

    assertTrue(mNavBuilder.mIntentList.isEmpty());
}
</code></pre>

Q: Reading chunks of a text file with a Java 8 Stream A: <p>Here's a Java 24 solution that uses a custom <a href="https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/24/docs/api/java.base/java/util/stream/Gatherer.html" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><code>Gatherer</code></a> to gather an initial <code>Stream&lt;String&gt;</code> of lines into a <code>Stream&lt;String&gt;</code> of chunks of lines between delimiter lines.</p>
<pre class="lang-java prettyprint-override"><code>String filePath = &quot;/path/to/dollar-delimited.txt&quot;;

Supplier&lt;StringBuilder&gt; initializer = StringBuilder::new;
Gatherer.Integrator.Greedy&lt;StringBuilder, String, String&gt; integrator =
        (state, element, downstream) -&gt; {
            if (&quot;$$$$&quot;.equals(element)) {
                String downstreamElement = state.toString();
                state.setLength(0);
                return downstream.push(downstreamElement);
            } else {
                state.append(element);
                state.append(&quot;\n&quot;);
                return true;
            }
        };
BiConsumer&lt;StringBuilder, Gatherer.Downstream&lt;? super String&gt;&gt; finisher =
        (state, downstream) -&gt; {
            if (!state.isEmpty()) downstream.push(state.toString());
        };
Gatherer&lt;String, StringBuilder, String&gt; gatherer = 
        Gatherer.ofSequential(initializer, integrator, finisher);

try (Stream&lt;String&gt; stream =
             Files.lines(Paths.get(filePath)).gather(gatherer)) {

    // Do whatever you need to do with the stream of chunks
    stream.forEach(chunk -&gt; System.out.println(chunk + &quot;==========&quot;));
}
</code></pre>
<h1>Example</h1>
<h2>Input:</h2>
<pre class="lang-none prettyprint-override"><code>line 1
line 2
line 3
line 4
$$$$
line 5
line 6
$$$$
</code></pre>
<h2>Output:</h2>
<pre class="lang-none prettyprint-override"><code>line 1
line 2
line 3
line 4
==========
line 5
line 6
==========
</code></pre>
